VibeSolaris optional system configuration directory

This directory is used only when it is writable by the current account. If it is not writable, VibeSolaris automatically stores that account's encrypted configuration under ~/.vibesolaris instead.

===========================================

At runtime VibeSolaris can create these files here:

  config.enc   Encrypted system-wide provider/configuration data.
  master.key   256-bit machine key encoded as hex.

Both files are created with mode 0600 and the directory with mode 0700 by
default.  Creating them under /etc normally requires root privileges.

The encrypted file uses AES-256-CBC with encrypt-then-MAC HMAC-SHA256.
Separate encryption and authentication keys are derived from the 256-bit
machine key.  The key is never written into config.enc.

For managed installations the master key can instead be supplied through the
VIBESOLARIS_MASTER_KEY environment variable as exactly 64 hexadecimal
characters.  In that mode master.key does not need to exist.

Administrators who deliberately want several users to share the same global
credentials should grant access through a dedicated OS group/ACL rather than
making master.key world-readable.

VibeSolaris 0.10.2 autosaves provider selection, per-provider models and API
credentials, protocol URLs, cache setting, and MCP server definitions to
config.enc whenever those settings change and this directory is writable.
MCP remote bearer tokens are therefore encrypted at rest with the same system
configuration mechanism.